{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/TightlipCore\/documentation\/TightlipCore"]]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/TightlipCore\/documentation\/TightlipCore\/SectionedConfigs","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Declare staging and production secrets in one file and select between them per build."}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Tightlip"}],"roleHeading":"Article","title":"Multi-Environment Configs","role":"article"},"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"kind":"article","primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"text":"When to Use Sectioned Configs","level":2,"anchor":"When-to-Use-Sectioned-Configs","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Reach for sectioned configs when the same property names need different values across environments — staging keys for development builds, production keys for release builds, perhaps a ","type":"text"},{"code":"qa","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" set for a release-candidate lane.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A flat config has no environment concept. If you have one set of values, stay flat.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Format","level":2,"anchor":"Format","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Each top-level identifier followed by ","type":"text"},{"code":":","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (with no value) is an environment section. Lines within a section are indented exactly 2 spaces:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"yaml","code":["# Secrets.yml","staging:","  revenueCatAPIKey: STAGING_REVENUECAT_API_KEY","  hmacSigningKey:   STAGING_HMAC_KEY","","production:","  revenueCatAPIKey: PROD_REVENUECAT_API_KEY","  hmacSigningKey:   PROD_HMAC_KEY"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"All sections must declare the same set of property names.","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" Mismatched property sets fail at parse time — this prevents a release build from accidentally referencing a property that only exists in staging.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The active section is chosen at build time. For the rules — "},{"code":"TIGHTLIP_ENV","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", Xcode "},{"code":"CONFIGURATION","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", the auto-inference behavior — see "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TightlipCore\/documentation\/TightlipCore\/EnvironmentSelection","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Naming-Convention-for-Env-Vars","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Naming Convention for Env Vars"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Devs working on several apps on the same machine see bare names like "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"REVENUECAT_API_KEY"},{"type":"text","text":" collide. Prefix every env var with an app-specific tag — "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"<APP_PREFIX>_<SECRET>"},{"type":"text","text":" in screaming snake case (e.g. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ACME_REVENUECAT_API_KEY"},{"type":"text","text":"). Tightlip doesn’t enforce this; the convention just keeps configs across projects from stepping on each other."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The Swift-side property name (","type":"text"},{"code":"revenueCatAPIKey","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") stays clean either way — only the env-var side gets the prefix.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Related-Documentation","title":"Related Documentation","identifiers":["doc:\/\/TightlipCore\/documentation\/TightlipCore\/EnvironmentSelection","doc:\/\/TightlipCore\/documentation\/TightlipCore\/ConfigGrammar"]},{"anchor":"How-To-Guides","title":"How-To Guides","identifiers":["doc:\/\/TightlipCore\/documentation\/TightlipCore\/EnvFileDirective"],"generated":true}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/tightlipcore\/sectionedconfigs"]}],"references":{"doc://TightlipCore/documentation/TightlipCore/EnvironmentSelection":{"url":"\/documentation\/tightlipcore\/environmentselection","title":"Environment Selection","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/TightlipCore\/documentation\/TightlipCore\/EnvironmentSelection","abstract":[{"text":"How Tightlip picks the active section for a sectioned config.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","role":"article"},"doc://TightlipCore/documentation/TightlipCore/EnvFileDirective":{"title":"Overriding the Sourced Env File","kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/tightlipcore\/envfiledirective","abstract":[{"text":"Point Tightlip at a different shell-init file with the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"envFile:"},{"text":" directive.","type":"text"}],"role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/TightlipCore\/documentation\/TightlipCore\/EnvFileDirective","type":"topic"},"doc://TightlipCore/documentation/TightlipCore":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A SwiftPM build-tool plugin that generates a typed Swift "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Secrets"},{"type":"text","text":" enum from environment variables at build time."}],"title":"Tightlip","identifier":"doc:\/\/TightlipCore\/documentation\/TightlipCore","url":"\/documentation\/tightlipcore","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","role":"collection"},"doc://TightlipCore/documentation/TightlipCore/ConfigGrammar":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TightlipCore\/documentation\/TightlipCore\/ConfigGrammar","title":"Config Grammar","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"The accepted shape of ","type":"text"},{"code":"Secrets.yml","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", line by line.","type":"text"}],"role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/tightlipcore\/configgrammar","kind":"article"}}}